{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210736,"nonce":"qCgTDC4SNmb/LT+1n0Q6sqm+I1s=","title":"ObjFiber.jit_resume_value + krio_* fields invisible to GC and unbarriered","message":"Fixed in commit 4386add. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\nObjFiber gained three new Value-typed fields after the original GC sweep was authored:\n- `jit_resume_value: Option\u003cValue\u003e` — written by `vm_interp.rs::resume_caller` every time a child fiber resumes its parent through the JIT barrier path.\n- `krio_return_value: Value` (cfg `host`) — written by the krio-fiber body when it completes.\n- `krio_jit_roots: Vec\u003cValue\u003e` (cfg `host`) — snapshot of JIT_ROOTS_STORE on yield, restored on resume.\n\nNONE of these were covered by the four ObjFiber arms in `src/runtime/gc.rs`:\n- `trace_object` (~2093)\n- `update_pointers_in_object_inline` (~2376)\n- `check_old_obj_barriers` (~907)\n- `validate_no_nursery_ptrs_inline` (~1832)\n\nCombined with **no write_barrier on the resume_caller writes** and **plugin_abi.rs's `let _ = vm`** (so `wlift_plugin_list_add` / `wlift_plugin_map_set` never barrier either), a young Value stored into an old-gen Fiber (or old-gen plugin container) was both untraced AND not enrolled in the remembered_set. Minor GC freed it; ~30 s later the freelist recycled the slot and free() tripped on a non-allocated pointer.\n\n**Why nature-garden hit it reliably:** outer game-loop fiber resumes a per-frame child fiber (Fiber.try in Game.run) → every frame writes a young Value into the parent's jit_resume_value. Plugins (@hatch:gpu/image/window/physics) append/store Wren-side Values into long-lived host containers via the ABI shim entrypoints. Both channels fire on every frame.\n\n**Why:** every author of a new ObjFiber field or plugin entrypoint must update FOUR places (three GC visitors + writer-site barrier). The cross-cutting pattern is \"new field → forget one of the four sites → silent UAF that surfaces after first promotion + ~5s of allocations.\"\n\n**How to apply:** any future ObjFiber field of type `Value` / `Vec\u003cValue\u003e` / `Option\u003cValue\u003e` MUST appear in all four `gc.rs` Fiber arms. Any plugin_abi.rs entrypoint that stores a Value into a heap container MUST `vm_ref(vm)` and `vm.gc.write_barrier(container_hdr, value)`. Pattern: copy from `src/capi.rs::wrenSetMapValue` (3010-3037) which is canonical.\n\nFixes landed 2026-06-06:\n- `src/runtime/gc.rs` — four Fiber arms cover jit_resume_value + krio_* under `cfg(feature = \"host\")`\n- `src/runtime/vm_interp.rs::resume_caller` — barrier both jit_resume_value writes\n- `src/plugin_abi.rs::wlift_plugin_list_add` + `wlift_plugin_map_set` — vm_ref + barrier (drop the `let _ = vm`)\n- `src/codegen/runtime_fns.rs::make_closure_inner` — refresh closure pointer from JIT root every upvalue write + barrier each upvalue store (the stale-pointer-after-promotion bug was a separate channel hitting tier-up'd per-frame closures)\n\nRelated (same channel, earlier fixes): [[project-jit-list-subscript-set-barrier]], [[project-fiber-set-reg-barrier]], and the `list_swap` + `get_or_init_context_map` fixes from 2026-06-04.\n\nWorkflow output that surfaced this: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-amaterasu-Vibranium-wren-lift/ca17a31a-a0da-4f6d-8102-ea6c1db8c8ab/tasks/wt8tq33tn.output` — 52/55 verified bugs, ranked.","files":null}]}